# Copy to `.env` (which is gitignored) and fill in. Nothing reads this file
# automatically — source it into your shell before a live run:
#
#     set -a; . ./.env; set +a          # bash / git bash
#
# OUTCOME reads these from the environment only, and never writes a credential
# to disk.

# From https://dashboard.heycall-e.com/account/api-keys
CALLE_API_KEY=

# Every number the agent is permitted to dial, comma separated, E.164.
# The agent finds numbers on calls and will try to ring them, so this is the
# list that decides whose phone can actually ring. For a first live run, put
# exactly one number in it: your own.
CALLE_ALLOWED_NUMBERS=+447700900123

# Optional. Only for reaching a CALL-E staging host; the credential is refused
# for anywhere else.
# CALLE_BASE_URL=https://api.heycall-e.com

# Optional. Lets the goal interpreter use a model instead of the regex rules.
# Absent, it falls back to the rules and the run is unaffected.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
